<item>
            <title>[LU-20485] Use LLVM automatic reference counting</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20485</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;We might be able to use LLVM&apos;s automatic reference counting to find ref count bugs in our kernel code. While this feature was originally designed for Objective-C, the annotations work fine on C. I was able to discover a few small bugs with this. This warrants more discussion with the upstream Linux/LLVM maintainers to understand if there is a path to adoption in the Linux kernel.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In the meantime, this ticket will track those bug fixes along with the PoC implementation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;1&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://clang.llvm.org/docs/AutomaticReferenceCounting.html&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://clang.llvm.org/docs/AutomaticReferenceCounting.html&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
